WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.472 --> 00:00:02.509
- One day all of this will be yours.

00:00:02.509 --> 00:00:04.026
The other people who are spending

00:00:04.026 --> 00:00:05.520
their whole time on ego trips.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.037
We've configured society in such a way

00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:09.719
that so many things can be bought.

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:11.367
Well if you're giving back

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:12.719
you took too much.

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:15.400
And human beings don't do
scary things on their own.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.863
There's nothing in nature
that grows indefinitely

00:00:17.863 --> 00:00:18.849
except cancer.

00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:20.280
How many people do you
know that in their deathbed

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.997
said, "Boy I wish I had spent
more time at the office."

00:00:22.997 --> 00:00:24.932
They say this seems to be out of control,

00:00:24.932 --> 00:00:26.061
pull the reins.

00:00:26.061 --> 00:00:28.171
And letting it sit there
and not doing it is

00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:29.495
an important part.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.225
What am I doing this for?

00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:34.738
- He is the CEO and majority
owner of Semco Partners.

00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:37.651
Under his leadership the
business grew from four million

00:00:37.651 --> 00:00:40.902
dollars to 212 million dollars.

00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:43.341
His innovative management
policies have attracted

00:00:43.341 --> 00:00:45.991
widespread interest from around the world.

00:00:45.991 --> 00:00:48.194
He's Ricardo Semler and here are his

00:00:48.194 --> 00:00:50.361
top ten rules for success.

00:00:52.994 --> 00:00:55.487
- I taught MBAs at MIT for a time

00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:58.267
and I ended up one day at
the Mount Auburn cemetery

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.930
it was beautiful cemetery in Cambridge.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:01.965
And I was walking around,
it was my birthday,

00:01:01.965 --> 00:01:03.772
and I was thinking.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:05.781
And the first time around
I saw these tombstones

00:01:05.781 --> 00:01:08.529
and these wonderful people
who do done great things

00:01:08.529 --> 00:01:12.512
and I thought, what do I
want to be remembered for?

00:01:12.512 --> 00:01:14.052
And I did another stroll around

00:01:14.052 --> 00:01:16.010
and the second time
another question came to me

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:19.233
which did did me better, which was,

00:01:19.233 --> 00:01:21.889
why do I want to be remembered at all?

00:01:21.889 --> 00:01:23.924
(laughing)

00:01:23.924 --> 00:01:26.603
And that, I think, took
me different places.

00:01:26.603 --> 00:01:29.655
When I was 50, my wife and
I had a nice (mumbling)

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:30.704
for a whole afternoon.

00:01:30.704 --> 00:01:32.903
We had a big pit with fire

00:01:32.903 --> 00:01:36.526
and I threw everything I had
ever done into that fire .

00:01:36.526 --> 00:01:38.747
This is a book in 38 languages,

00:01:38.747 --> 00:01:41.295
hundreds and hundreds
of articles and DVDs.

00:01:41.295 --> 00:01:42.685
Everything there was.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:44.130
And that did two things.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:47.382
One, it freed our five kids from following

00:01:47.382 --> 00:01:49.380
in the steps of shadow of,

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.651
they don't know what I do.

00:01:51.651 --> 00:01:53.835
(laughing)
Which is good.

00:01:53.835 --> 00:01:56.178
And I'm not going to take
them someone say, "One day

00:01:56.178 --> 00:01:57.622
"all of this will be yours."

00:01:57.622 --> 00:02:01.289
So the five kids know
nothing which is good.

00:02:02.683 --> 00:02:05.715
And the second thing is I freed myself

00:02:05.715 --> 00:02:08.494
from this anchor of past achievement

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:11.478
or whatever it is and I'm
free to start something new.

00:02:11.478 --> 00:02:14.033
Every time and to decide
things from scratch.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.471
I think that a certain amount of ego

00:02:17.471 --> 00:02:20.864
and vanity and self-esteem
is absolutely necessary.

00:02:20.864 --> 00:02:22.898
I don't think it's possible for you to

00:02:22.898 --> 00:02:23.731
to keep a

00:02:26.527 --> 00:02:28.168
a structured personality

00:02:28.168 --> 00:02:31.018
with you giving up ego
and vanity and everything.

00:02:31.018 --> 00:02:33.418
It's yourself, that is
that small percentage

00:02:33.418 --> 00:02:35.560
of religious people or people or Hermits,

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:40.408
or people who are able to
go to that that extent.

00:02:40.408 --> 00:02:42.359
As on the other hand, the other people

00:02:42.359 --> 00:02:44.581
who are spending their
whole time on ego trips

00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:46.079
and making sure that they show up

00:02:46.079 --> 00:02:47.896
and their photograph is in the paper.

00:02:47.896 --> 00:02:49.625
And they go to be seen and be seen.

00:02:49.625 --> 00:02:52.491
And I'm not in any of these
in any of these situations.

00:02:52.491 --> 00:02:56.106
So I'm constantly
managing the issue of ego

00:02:56.106 --> 00:02:58.723
and asking myself, why am I doing this?

00:02:58.723 --> 00:03:02.359
Am I doing this, is it
enough of a message?

00:03:02.359 --> 00:03:03.997
Is it important?

00:03:03.997 --> 00:03:06.349
Do I do a few very very select of these?

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:08.542
Or do I do it all the
time just to make sure

00:03:08.542 --> 00:03:12.575
that I'm I'm busy, I'm
in the news or whatever.

00:03:12.575 --> 00:03:14.349
I don't do the second part

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:17.086
because the amount of things
I refuse per day is enormous.

00:03:17.086 --> 00:03:20.696
And so I am trying always
to manage that issue.

00:03:20.696 --> 00:03:23.446
But I think without this force of

00:03:24.377 --> 00:03:26.460
of ego which is within myself.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.637
So when I'm giving when I feel that

00:03:28.637 --> 00:03:31.274
I'm giving something anonymously.

00:03:31.274 --> 00:03:32.596
A school for example,

00:03:32.596 --> 00:03:34.654
that they will never know
that it was me who gave it.

00:03:34.654 --> 00:03:36.810
It is feeding my ego

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.043
to feel good about having done that.

00:03:39.043 --> 00:03:40.743
But it doesn't have my name on it,

00:03:40.743 --> 00:03:42.493
I don't show up there so it
doesn't have that second part

00:03:42.493 --> 00:03:44.342
of the ego which I don't think I need.

00:03:44.342 --> 00:03:47.657
And I needed more in the
past and I started to

00:03:47.657 --> 00:03:49.539
tame it as the years go by.

00:03:49.539 --> 00:03:51.144
And so it's a very delicate exercise

00:03:51.144 --> 00:03:55.080
but I think the people without that first

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:58.703
need to express themselves
or to have the ego issue

00:03:58.703 --> 00:04:01.760
balanced end up doing very little as well.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.738
- Mm-hmm.
- For the very

00:04:02.738 --> 00:04:04.552
little publicly, of course.

00:04:04.552 --> 00:04:05.997
That's what we're talking about.

00:04:05.997 --> 00:04:09.138
For me, the idea of success,

00:04:09.138 --> 00:04:12.131
power, and money together
has never been a motto.

00:04:12.131 --> 00:04:14.214
It was just a realization

00:04:16.078 --> 00:04:20.119
that this was so important
to people in general.

00:04:20.119 --> 00:04:24.784
But success, the idea that
success is connected to money

00:04:24.784 --> 00:04:27.997
to me is really a strange combination.

00:04:27.997 --> 00:04:28.830
It's

00:04:29.677 --> 00:04:33.066
there's a very small correlation

00:04:33.066 --> 00:04:36.221
between success and money, in any case

00:04:36.221 --> 00:04:40.147
there's a strong correlation
between money and power

00:04:40.147 --> 00:04:42.884
because we've configured
society in such a way

00:04:42.884 --> 00:04:46.458
that so many things can be bought.

00:04:46.458 --> 00:04:50.546
But success fits into
another the other Trinity

00:04:50.546 --> 00:04:54.479
of balance, of security certainly because

00:04:54.479 --> 00:04:56.845
it was much more secure in our society

00:04:56.845 --> 00:04:59.422
to have a bank account than to have none.

00:04:59.422 --> 00:05:01.631
But it's not by any means that

00:05:01.631 --> 00:05:04.889
this will enable you in any of the other

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:06.520
in any of the other factors.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:09.623
But I think the people
that imagine that success,

00:05:09.623 --> 00:05:12.128
money, power etcetera are

00:05:12.128 --> 00:05:15.424
useful only believe in this for a while

00:05:15.424 --> 00:05:16.986
it's very difficult to
imagine that somebody

00:05:16.986 --> 00:05:18.844
believes in this over the long run

00:05:18.844 --> 00:05:21.277
because there's so many opportunities

00:05:21.277 --> 00:05:23.505
and examples to see that there are so

00:05:23.505 --> 00:05:26.264
many important things that you
can't buy with any of this.

00:05:26.264 --> 00:05:28.926
I accumulated a lot of
money when I think about it

00:05:28.926 --> 00:05:31.195
you when you think and you say,

00:05:31.195 --> 00:05:32.894
"Now is the time to give back."

00:05:32.894 --> 00:05:33.727
Well if you're giving
back, you took too much.

00:05:33.727 --> 00:05:35.977
(laughing)

00:05:38.219 --> 00:05:40.469
(applause)

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.629
I see, I keep thinking of Warren Buffett

00:05:46.629 --> 00:05:48.125
waking up one day and finding out that

00:05:48.125 --> 00:05:50.996
he has 30 billion dollars
more than he thought he had.

00:05:50.996 --> 00:05:52.336
And he looks and says. "what
am I going to do with this?"

00:05:52.336 --> 00:05:54.707
He said, "Let me give it to
somebody who really needs this.

00:05:54.707 --> 00:05:56.097
"I'll give it to Bill Gates."

00:05:56.097 --> 00:05:58.347
(laughing)

00:05:59.468 --> 00:06:02.403
And, my guy, who is my
financial adviser in New York,

00:06:02.403 --> 00:06:04.482
he says, "Look you're
not you're a silly guy

00:06:04.482 --> 00:06:07.689
"because you would have
4.1 times more money today

00:06:07.689 --> 00:06:10.108
"if you had made money with money

00:06:10.108 --> 00:06:11.748
"instead of sharing as you go."

00:06:11.748 --> 00:06:13.672
But I like sharing as you go better.

00:06:13.672 --> 00:06:15.372
Our past is very determinant.

00:06:15.372 --> 00:06:18.598
When you think about Europe
or the Western hemisphere,

00:06:18.598 --> 00:06:22.502
in general, we are stuck
by issues of the past.

00:06:22.502 --> 00:06:24.790
It is the past that holds back.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:28.676
You know, and if you said that you were as

00:06:28.676 --> 00:06:31.115
I've done in the past, you
said let me burn everything,

00:06:31.115 --> 00:06:33.023
let me get rid of everything in the past

00:06:33.023 --> 00:06:35.740
you you're free to start
thinking about the future.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.990
But if you're still collecting the past

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:41.044
and looking to the past as a solution

00:06:41.044 --> 00:06:44.259
having history is a very strong anchor,

00:06:44.259 --> 00:06:46.218
you're unable to move forward

00:06:46.218 --> 00:06:49.084
because there are historical
reasons why our tribe

00:06:49.084 --> 00:06:52.165
of humanity is such a slow changer because

00:06:52.165 --> 00:06:54.332
change is very very scary.

00:06:55.446 --> 00:06:58.887
And human beings don't do
scary things on their own.

00:06:58.887 --> 00:07:03.054
They take something much bigger
to force them into change.

00:07:06.049 --> 00:07:08.309
- [Man] What kind of
big thing would that be?

00:07:08.309 --> 00:07:11.124
- For every human being individual

00:07:11.124 --> 00:07:13.623
it's the heart attack, the car accident,

00:07:13.623 --> 00:07:16.922
the something that happened
which was much bigger than you.

00:07:16.922 --> 00:07:19.057
Which suddenly you wake
up and say, "Oh my God

00:07:19.057 --> 00:07:21.087
"I've been spending all
my life inside a box

00:07:21.087 --> 00:07:22.871
"just working for someone else.

00:07:22.871 --> 00:07:25.010
"Oh isn't there a better way?"

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:28.058
For humanity, in general, it is this that

00:07:28.058 --> 00:07:31.673
suddenly it stops raining,
suddenly everything goes crazy

00:07:31.673 --> 00:07:34.017
and you can't control the climate.

00:07:34.017 --> 00:07:35.694
So that's big enough.

00:07:35.694 --> 00:07:39.146
If the world were hit by a
meteorite it would be enough.

00:07:39.146 --> 00:07:40.857
It takes enormous things like that.

00:07:40.857 --> 00:07:43.394
So we are a bit, didn't
dinosaurs in that sense

00:07:43.394 --> 00:07:46.516
that we will roam around and do our thing

00:07:46.516 --> 00:07:49.182
until we're hit by something
much bigger than us.

00:07:49.182 --> 00:07:51.014
And that's true even
for the individual who

00:07:51.014 --> 00:07:52.891
needs a heart attack to wake up to find

00:07:52.891 --> 00:07:54.829
out that they've been working too much.

00:07:54.829 --> 00:07:57.426
- In each block of time
your company has grown,

00:07:57.426 --> 00:07:58.862
your profits have grown,

00:07:58.862 --> 00:08:00.858
your own personal wealth has grown.

00:08:00.858 --> 00:08:03.309
A company that might
have had a few hundred

00:08:03.309 --> 00:08:04.534
now has 5,000.

00:08:04.534 --> 00:08:08.766
What is it in all of
that still motivates you?

00:08:08.766 --> 00:08:11.177
Is it about the growth,
is it about being bigger,

00:08:11.177 --> 00:08:12.880
and feeling good about yourself because

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.621
you've run something like that?

00:08:14.621 --> 00:08:16.593
- No, as a matter of fact, now we've had

00:08:16.593 --> 00:08:20.450
a few opportunities to sell to partners.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:22.687
Our part completely and
I'm very happy to do that

00:08:22.687 --> 00:08:25.717
in a thousand people, or 2,000
people will go at a stretch.

00:08:25.717 --> 00:08:27.601
No, I think I've gotten over that.

00:08:27.601 --> 00:08:29.739
There's something in the
beginning of a career where you

00:08:29.739 --> 00:08:31.011
where you find that important.

00:08:31.011 --> 00:08:32.509
But the you realize
that there's nothing in

00:08:32.509 --> 00:08:35.643
nature that grows
indefinitely except cancer.

00:08:35.643 --> 00:08:37.464
You know, everything else
and you have the tall

00:08:37.464 --> 00:08:40.497
poppy syndrome rationale
here in Australia.

00:08:40.497 --> 00:08:43.267
The tree that grows most
is the one that's first

00:08:43.267 --> 00:08:44.571
struck by lightning.

00:08:44.571 --> 00:08:46.659
This is the idea that you
grow more, you have more money

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:49.675
and you become better
is very very silly idea.

00:08:49.675 --> 00:08:53.690
And so, what takes me let's
say, from business to education

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.657
or to dealing with
two-year-olds is that I'm

00:08:55.657 --> 00:08:58.244
interested in human nature and why we do

00:08:58.244 --> 00:08:59.545
some of the silly things we do is

00:08:59.545 --> 00:09:01.038
there's not a better way to do this.

00:09:01.038 --> 00:09:04.103
I always come back to variations of the

00:09:04.103 --> 00:09:07.512
the question that my my son
asked me when he was three.

00:09:07.512 --> 00:09:10.187
We're sitting in a Jacuzzi and he said,

00:09:10.187 --> 00:09:11.736
"Dad, why do we exist?"

00:09:11.736 --> 00:09:13.654
There is no other question,

00:09:13.654 --> 00:09:14.840
nobody has any other question.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:18.778
You have variations of this one
question from three onwards.

00:09:18.778 --> 00:09:22.441
And so, when you spend time in a company,

00:09:22.441 --> 00:09:24.375
in a bureaucracy, in an organization

00:09:24.375 --> 00:09:26.744
and you're you're saying,
boy, how many people

00:09:26.744 --> 00:09:28.381
do you know that in their deathbed

00:09:28.381 --> 00:09:30.888
said, "Boy I wish I had spent
more time at the office."

00:09:30.888 --> 00:09:33.722
So there's a whole thing of

00:09:33.722 --> 00:09:36.200
having the courage now,

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:38.075
not in a week, not in two months.

00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:40.385
No not when you find
out you have something.

00:09:40.385 --> 00:09:43.341
To say no, what am I doing this for?

00:09:43.341 --> 00:09:45.322
Stop everything, let me do something else

00:09:45.322 --> 00:09:46.608
and it'll be okay.

00:09:46.608 --> 00:09:48.881
It'll be much better
than what you're doing

00:09:48.881 --> 00:09:50.991
if you're stuck in a process.

00:09:50.991 --> 00:09:53.127
So when you think about the fact that we

00:09:53.127 --> 00:09:55.943
allocate the same amount of hours,

00:09:55.943 --> 00:09:58.995
what is it that that we need to do

00:09:58.995 --> 00:10:00.134
or we can do?

00:10:00.134 --> 00:10:02.209
It's very easy today to
set up organizations.

00:10:02.209 --> 00:10:03.874
That's the way we're set up.

00:10:03.874 --> 00:10:06.865
Where we don't want to
know how many people work.

00:10:06.865 --> 00:10:09.046
We don't want to know
exactly how many hours

00:10:09.046 --> 00:10:10.121
each person works.

00:10:10.121 --> 00:10:12.535
We're going to negotiate with the group

00:10:12.535 --> 00:10:15.428
or with a person for a certain result.

00:10:15.428 --> 00:10:17.438
If the person is able
to do it in three hours

00:10:17.438 --> 00:10:19.219
or four hours or seven hours

00:10:19.219 --> 00:10:20.295
we don't want to know.

00:10:20.295 --> 00:10:22.149
We don't want that control anymore.

00:10:22.149 --> 00:10:23.445
We want to be able to say,

00:10:23.445 --> 00:10:25.735
"Look, if you can distribute your life

00:10:25.735 --> 00:10:28.379
"differently in terms of where you are

00:10:28.379 --> 00:10:30.265
"or the amount of hours
you work or between

00:10:30.265 --> 00:10:33.698
"idleness and leisure and the rest of the

00:10:33.698 --> 00:10:35.473
"things you want to do."

00:10:35.473 --> 00:10:39.746
The framework that's available
today already permits that.

00:10:39.746 --> 00:10:40.965
It's just companies that are not

00:10:40.965 --> 00:10:43.220
letting go because they
think they need control.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:45.760
They want to know if the
person showed up et cetera

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:47.068
because otherwise it's
unfair for the other one

00:10:47.068 --> 00:10:48.518
who worked more hours.

00:10:48.518 --> 00:10:50.154
And that's an obsolete rationale

00:10:50.154 --> 00:10:51.328
it's an obsolete system.

00:10:51.328 --> 00:10:53.944
And so, it's perfectly possible and that's

00:10:53.944 --> 00:10:56.728
how we work is to say, "Give me this

00:10:56.728 --> 00:10:58.803
"by such and such a date."

00:10:58.803 --> 00:11:00.229
And then if it's more hours less hours

00:11:00.229 --> 00:11:01.878
or where you do it is none of our concern.

00:11:01.878 --> 00:11:04.256
And that solves the issue of

00:11:04.256 --> 00:11:06.201
allocating too many hours

00:11:06.201 --> 00:11:08.872
when today we don't need
that many in order to produce

00:11:08.872 --> 00:11:10.058
the same thing.

00:11:10.058 --> 00:11:13.224
In a time in which things seem to be lost

00:11:13.224 --> 00:11:15.050
in terms of control and direction

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.890
the first reaction is the same one

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.280
is you have with a horse.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.491
When you're riding a horse and the horse

00:11:20.491 --> 00:11:24.438
is going downhill and
it starts speeding up

00:11:24.438 --> 00:11:25.867
and losing control

00:11:25.867 --> 00:11:27.387
you pull the reins which is the very

00:11:27.387 --> 00:11:28.955
worst thing you could ever do.

00:11:28.955 --> 00:11:31.700
Because then the horse
has to pull up their head

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:34.228
and try to go down with
you pulling the rein there

00:11:34.228 --> 00:11:35.311
because you're afraid.

00:11:35.311 --> 00:11:36.890
This is the same thing
that happens in these

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:39.007
organizations, it's been
happening in the companies.

00:11:39.007 --> 00:11:40.775
They say this seems to be out of control,

00:11:40.775 --> 00:11:42.778
pull the reins together

00:11:42.778 --> 00:11:46.168
and let's get control of
this thing that we're losing.

00:11:46.168 --> 00:11:48.396
And the fact is the more you do that

00:11:48.396 --> 00:11:50.729
the more you have an entity,

00:11:52.265 --> 00:11:55.300
an organism, an organization
that doesn't know

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.911
what to do and is frightened.

00:11:56.911 --> 00:12:00.329
And so this fear, this malice
that's there in society

00:12:00.329 --> 00:12:03.750
today, needs a completely
different organization

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:06.447
is a completely different
architecture than this one

00:12:06.447 --> 00:12:09.337
of more and more and more
control and more slaves

00:12:09.337 --> 00:12:10.415
building up something for you.

00:12:10.415 --> 00:12:13.642
It needs something that
says give up the reins

00:12:13.642 --> 00:12:16.798
and realize that once
the horse has control

00:12:16.798 --> 00:12:20.911
and the head is free, that
you're able then to use

00:12:20.911 --> 00:12:23.900
the best qualities of knowing
where to step in the things

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.926
that came naturally and that
came tribally already within

00:12:26.926 --> 00:12:29.857
is, many of which are much wiser than the

00:12:29.857 --> 00:12:32.024
smart decision of control.

00:12:32.889 --> 00:12:34.725
- [Man] Control is smart

00:12:34.725 --> 00:12:35.826
but it's not wise?

00:12:35.826 --> 00:12:37.543
- Yeah control always seems smart

00:12:37.543 --> 00:12:39.537
it seems intelligent to say ah,

00:12:39.537 --> 00:12:41.940
so you tell me where you
were, you tell me this,

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.286
you tell me how much you
spent, you come here.

00:12:44.286 --> 00:12:45.760
You all come from everywhere around

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:47.576
from 50 kilometers away

00:12:47.576 --> 00:12:50.165
and you take subways, and you take buses

00:12:50.165 --> 00:12:52.678
and you spend three
hours a day in traffic.

00:12:52.678 --> 00:12:54.155
But once you come here

00:12:54.155 --> 00:12:55.958
I can control you, I
know whether you're here,

00:12:55.958 --> 00:12:57.966
I know whether you came on time.

00:12:57.966 --> 00:13:00.667
I have a boarding-school mentality really

00:13:00.667 --> 00:13:01.780
of control.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.693
So if I send my kids over there and I know

00:13:03.693 --> 00:13:05.151
that they're going to wake up

00:13:05.151 --> 00:13:07.114
and they're going to go to
mathematics and then biology

00:13:07.114 --> 00:13:08.391
said they're going to be great.

00:13:08.391 --> 00:13:10.786
It seems smart, but it's very unwise.

00:13:10.786 --> 00:13:12.570
You have kids who then leave that

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:15.431
and who's thought they've
wasted half their life there.

00:13:15.431 --> 00:13:19.282
And then they want to do away
with all of this organization

00:13:19.282 --> 00:13:21.016
that was in place before.

00:13:21.016 --> 00:13:23.683
Well you know I had a I had this

00:13:24.633 --> 00:13:29.395
unsuccessful career as a rock
guitarist which was wonderful.

00:13:29.395 --> 00:13:32.035
I mean, it was a wonderful
period of my life.

00:13:32.035 --> 00:13:33.820
But it was very interesting because

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.070
it showed where

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:38.278
where the limitations are

00:13:38.278 --> 00:13:40.758
and why sometimes you want to do

00:13:40.758 --> 00:13:43.258
something because you want to.

00:13:43.258 --> 00:13:47.022
But the combination of
talent and time is not right.

00:13:47.022 --> 00:13:49.309
And letting it sit there and not doing it

00:13:49.309 --> 00:13:51.149
is an important part.

00:13:51.149 --> 00:13:53.872
We've all learned how
to go on Sunday night

00:13:53.872 --> 00:13:56.572
to go to the email and work from home.

00:13:56.572 --> 00:13:58.621
But very few of us have
learned how to go to the

00:13:58.621 --> 00:14:00.793
movies on Monday afternoon.

00:14:00.793 --> 00:14:03.232
And if we're looking for
wisdom we need to learn

00:14:03.232 --> 00:14:05.367
to do that as well.

00:14:05.367 --> 00:14:07.097
And so it's basically

00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:09.904
what we've done all of
these years is very simple

00:14:09.904 --> 00:14:11.855
is use the little tool which is

00:14:11.855 --> 00:14:13.088
ask three whys in a row.

00:14:13.088 --> 00:14:14.948
Because the first why you
always have a good answer.

00:14:14.948 --> 00:14:17.412
For the second why, it
starts getting difficult.

00:14:17.412 --> 00:14:19.399
By the third why you don't really know

00:14:19.399 --> 00:14:21.448
why you're doing what you're doing.

00:14:21.448 --> 00:14:24.959
And so, what I want to leave you with is

00:14:24.959 --> 00:14:27.002
the seed and the thought that maybe

00:14:27.002 --> 00:14:28.832
if you do this you will
come to the question,

00:14:28.832 --> 00:14:30.340
what for?

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.141
What am I doing this for?

00:14:32.141 --> 00:14:34.121
And hopefully, as a result of that,

00:14:34.121 --> 00:14:36.832
and over time, I hope that with this

00:14:36.832 --> 00:14:38.885
and that's what I'm wishing you

00:14:38.885 --> 00:14:40.965
you'll have a much wiser future.

00:14:40.965 --> 00:14:42.188
Thank you very much.

00:14:42.188 --> 00:14:43.327
